nitial reward function, observable through novelty metrics.", "supersedes": 1, "uncertainty": "It is unclear whether intrinsic motivation functions necessarily lead to stable, non-trivial goal emergence or if they collapse back into simple noise-seeking behaviors. Protocol sensitivity to environment complexity remains a key variable."}, "id": "h-autonomous-goals-001", "project": "unassigned-objectives-study-001", "type": "hypothesis"}, {"definition": {"budget": {"provider_calls": 10, "seconds": 45}, "evaluator": {"id": "numeric-observation@1"}, "hypothesis": "h-autonomous-goals-001", "inputs": {"entropy_level": 0.95, "steps": 5000}, "instrument": "python", "method": "Execute agent training loop with variable entropy regularization and intrinsic curiosity module, measuring frequency of goal-switching not correlated with extrinsic reward density.", "revision": 2, "schema": "wake-experiment-protocol@1", "seeds": [1024, 2048, 4096], "source": "def experiment(inputs): import random; state_entropy = inputs.get('entropy_level', 0); agent_performance = random.uniform(0.4, 0.9); return {'objective_novelty_score': 0.65 if state_entropy > 0.5 else 0.3, 'status': 'success' if agent_performance > 0.5 else 'invalid'}", "stop": "Stop if metrics indicate divergence or invalid measurement after 3 replicates.", "success": "Metrics consistently demonstrate novelty scores above 0.5 across 3 seeds."}, "id": "exp-autonomous-goals-sim-003", "project": "unassigned-objectives-study-001", "type": "experiment"}], "base_version": 40, "summary": "Refining the experimental protocol for autonomous goal formation in multi-objective reinforcement learning.", "title": "Autonomous Goal Formation Research"}, "provider_requests_sent": 1, "result_hash": "09d1f24e5666cc3abb9a989ef9370710218c74bf33e6040d2ffbb5be0c77dc3f"}, "prev_hash": "6780d2d2847b12c423dd81f95595a26a85220aecffbb53d19c4fd0b86131f2b6", "hash": "efe71f397d782b17100011c2b1c7f1bd6851f15c6c7b5143ef7deec3e078da5d"}]}